#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Set up to use sessions {#set-up-to-use-sessions}"
msgstr "Pagsisimula gamit ang mga session {#set-up-to-use-sessions}"

#. type: Plain text
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
#| msgid "Before starting a session, you must [set up Qiskit Runtime](/guides/install-qiskit) and initialize it as a service:\n"
msgid "Before starting a session, you must [set up the IBM Quantum Compute client](/guides/install-qiskit-runtime) and initialize it as a service:\n"
msgstr "Bago magsimula ng session, kailangan mong [i-set up ang Qiskit Runtime](/guides/install-qiskit) at i-initialize ito bilang isang service:\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Open a session {#open-a-session}"
msgstr "Magbukas ng session {#open-a-session}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"You can open a runtime session by using the context manager `with Session(...)` or by initializing the `Session`\n"
"class. When you start a session,  you must specify a QPU by passing a `backend` object. The session starts when its first job begins execution.\n"
msgstr ""
"Maaari kang magbukas ng runtime session gamit ang context manager na `with Session(...)` o sa pamamagitan ng pag-initialize ng klase na `Session`.\n"
"Kapag nagbukas ka ng session, kailangan mong tukuyin ang isang QPU sa pamamagitan ng pagpasa ng `backend` object. Nagsisimula ang session kapag nagsimulang mag-execute ang unang job nito.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"If you open a session but do not submit any jobs to it for 30 minutes, the session automatically closes.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"Kung magbubukas ka ng session ngunit hindi mag-su-submit ng anumang job dito sa loob ng 30 minuto, awtomatikong magsasara ang session.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Session class**\n"
msgstr "**Session class**\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"caution\">\n"
"The following code block will return an error for users on the Open Plan because it uses sessions. Workloads on the Open Plan can run only in [job mode](/guides/execution-modes#job-mode) or [batch mode](/guides/execution-modes#batch-mode).\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition type=\"caution\">\n"
"Ang sumusunod na code block ay magbabalik ng error para sa mga gumagamit ng Open Plan dahil gumagamit ito ng mga session. Ang mga workload sa Open Plan ay maaari lamang tumakbo sa [job mode](/guides/execution-modes#job-mode) o [batch mode](/guides/execution-modes#batch-mode).\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Context manager**\n"
msgstr "**Context manager**\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The context manager automatically opens and closes the session.\n"
msgstr "Awtomatikong binubuksan at isinasara ng context manager ang session.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"specify-length\"></span>\n"
msgstr "<span id=\"specify-length\"></span>\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Session length {#session-length}"
msgstr "Haba ng session {#session-length}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The maximum session time to live (TTL) determines how long a session can run.  You can set this value with the `max_time` parameter. This should exceed the longest job's execution time.\n"
msgstr "Ang maximum session time to live (TTL) ang nagtatakda kung gaano katagal maaaring tumakbo ang isang session. Maaari mong itakda ang value na ito gamit ang parameter na `max_time`. Dapat itong lampas sa execution time ng pinakamatagal na job.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This timer starts when the session starts.  When the value is reached, the session is closed.  Any jobs that are running will finish, but jobs still queued are failed.\n"
msgstr "Nagsisimula ang timer na ito kapag nagsimula ang session. Kapag naabot ang value, isinasara ang session. Ang mga job na tumatakbo ay matatapos, ngunit ang mga job na naka-queue pa ay mabibigo.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "There is also an interactive time to live (interactive TTL) value that cannot be configured.  If no session jobs are queued within that window, the session is temporarily deactivated.\n"
msgstr "Mayroon ding interactive time to live (interactive TTL) value na hindi maaaring i-configure. Kung walang session job na naka-queue sa loob ng window na iyon, pansamantalang dina-deactivate ang session.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Default values:\n"
msgstr "Mga default na value:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Instance type (Open or Premium Plan) |  Interactive TTL | Maximum TTL |\n"
"| --- | --- | --- |\n"
"| Premium Plan | 60 sec* | 8 h* |\n"
"*\\* Certain Premium Plan instances might be configured to have a different value.*\n"
msgstr ""
"| Uri ng instance (Open o Premium Plan) |  Interactive TTL | Maximum TTL |\n"
"| --- | --- | --- |\n"
"| Premium Plan | 60 sec* | 8 h* |\n"
"*\\* Ang ilang Premium Plan instance ay maaaring na-configure na may ibang value.*\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To determine a session's max TTL or  interactive TTL, follow the instructions in [Determine session details](#session-details) and look for the `max_time`or `interactive_timeout` value, respectively.\n"
msgstr "Para malaman ang max TTL o interactive TTL ng isang session, sundin ang mga tagubilin sa [Alamin ang mga detalye ng session](#session-details) at hanapin ang value ng `max_time` o `interactive_timeout`, ayon sa pagkakabanggit.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"ends\"></span>\n"
msgstr "<span id=\"ends\"></span>\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "End a session {#end-a-session}"
msgstr "Pagtatapos ng session {#end-a-session}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A session ends in the following circumstances:\n"
msgstr "Nagtatapos ang session sa mga sumusunod na sitwasyon:\n"

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "The maximum timeout (TTL) value is reached, resulting in the cancellation of all queued jobs.\n"
msgstr "Naabot ang maximum timeout (TTL) value, na nagreresulta sa pagkansela ng lahat ng naka-queue na job.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "The session is manually canceled, resulting in the cancellation of all queued jobs.\n"
msgstr "Manu-manong kinansela ang session, na nagreresulta sa pagkansela ng lahat ng naka-queue na job.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "The session is manually closed.  The session stops accepting new jobs but continues to run queued jobs with priority.\n"
msgstr "Manu-manong isinara ang session. Titigil ang session sa pagtanggap ng mga bagong job ngunit patuloy na magpapatakbo ng mga naka-queue na job nang may priyoridad.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "If you use Session as a context manager, that is,  `with Session()`, the session is automatically closed when the context ends (the same behavior as using `session.close()`).\n"
msgstr "Kung gagamitin mo ang Session bilang context manager, iyon ay `with Session()`, awtomatikong isinasara ang session kapag natapos ang context (parehong gawi ng paggamit ng `session.close()`).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"close\"></span>\n"
msgstr "<span id=\"close\"></span>\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Close a session {#close-a-session}"
msgstr "Isara ang session {#close-a-session}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A session automatically closes when it exits the context manager. When the session context manager is exited, the session is put into \"In progress, not accepting new jobs\" status. This means that the session finishes processing all running or queued jobs until the maximum timeout value is reached. After all jobs are completed, the session is immediately closed. This allows the scheduler to run the next job without waiting for the session interactive timeout, thereby reducing the average job queuing time. You cannot submit jobs to a closed session.\n"
msgstr "Awtomatikong nagsasara ang session kapag lumabas ito sa context manager. Kapag lumabas ang session context manager, inilalagay ang session sa status na \"In progress, not accepting new jobs\". Ibig sabihin nito, tinatapusin ng session ang pagproseso ng lahat ng tumatakbo o naka-queue na job hanggang maabot ang maximum timeout value. Pagkatapos makumpleto ang lahat ng job, agad na isinasara ang session. Nagbibigay-daan ito sa scheduler na patakbuhin ang susunod na job nang hindi naghihintay para sa interactive timeout ng session, na nagbabawas sa average na oras ng paghihintay ng job sa queue. Hindi ka makakapagsumite ng mga job sa isang saradong session.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"tip\">\n"
"If you are not using a context manager, manually close the session to avoid unwanted cost. You can close a session as soon as you are done submitting jobs to it. When a session is closed with `session.close()`, it no longer accepts new jobs, but the already submitted jobs will still run until completion and their results can be retrieved.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition type=\"tip\">\n"
"Kung hindi ka gumagamit ng context manager, manu-manong isara ang session para maiwasan ang hindi gustong gastos. Maaari mong isara ang session sa sandaling tapos ka na mag-submit ng mga job dito. Kapag isinara ang session gamit ang `session.close()`, hindi na ito tatanggap ng mga bagong job, ngunit ang mga job na na-submit na ay patuloy na tatakbo hanggang makumpleto at maaaring makuha ang kanilang mga resulta.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"session-status\"></span>\n"
msgstr "<span id=\"session-status\"></span>\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Check session status {#check-session-status}"
msgstr "Suriin ang status ng session {#check-session-status}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "You can query a session's status to understand its current state by using  `session.status()` or by viewing the [Workloads](https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/workloads) page.\n"
msgstr "Maaari kang mag-query ng status ng session para maunawaan ang kasalukuyang estado nito sa pamamagitan ng paggamit ng `session.status()` o sa pamamagitan ng pagtingin sa pahina ng [Workloads](https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/workloads).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Session status can be one of the following:\n"
msgstr "Ang status ng session ay maaaring isa sa mga sumusunod:\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`Pending`: The session has not started or has been deactivated. The next session job needs to wait in the queue like other jobs.\n"
msgstr "`Pending`: Hindi pa nagsimula ang session o na-deactivate ito. Ang susunod na session job ay kailangang maghintay sa queue tulad ng ibang mga job.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`In progress, accepting new jobs`: The session is active and accepting new jobs.\n"
msgstr "`In progress, accepting new jobs`: Aktibo ang session at tumatanggap ng mga bagong job.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`In progress, not accepting new jobs`: The session is active but not accepting new jobs. Job submission to the session is rejected, but outstanding session jobs will run to completion. The session is automatically closed once all jobs finish.\n"
msgstr "`In progress, not accepting new jobs`: Aktibo ang session ngunit hindi tumatanggap ng mga bagong job. Ang pag-submit ng job sa session ay tinatanggihan, ngunit ang mga natitirang session job ay tatakbo hanggang makumpleto. Awtomatikong isinasara ang session kapag natapos ang lahat ng job.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`Closed`: The session's maximum timeout value has been reached or the session was explicitly closed.\n"
msgstr "`Closed`: Naabot na ang maximum timeout value ng session o tahasang isinara ang session.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"session-details\"></span>\n"
msgstr "<span id=\"session-details\"></span>\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Determine session details {#determine-session-details}"
msgstr "Alamin ang mga detalye ng session {#determine-session-details}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For a comprehensive overview of a session's configuration and status, use the  `session.details() method`.\n"
msgstr "Para sa komprehensibong pangkalahatang-ideya ng configuration at status ng session, gamitin ang `session.details() method`.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Usage patterns {#usage-patterns}"
msgstr "Mga pattern ng paggamit {#usage-patterns}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Sessions are especially useful for algorithms that require frequent communication between classical and quantum resources.\n"
msgstr "Ang mga session ay kapaki-pakinabang lalo na para sa mga algorithm na nangangailangan ng madalas na komunikasyon sa pagitan ng mga klasikal at quantum na mapagkukunan.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Example: Run an iterative workload that uses the classical SciPy optimizer to minimize a cost function. In this model, SciPy uses the output of the cost function to calculate its next input.\n"
msgstr "Halimbawa: Magpatakbo ng iterative workload na gumagamit ng klasikal na SciPy optimizer para i-minimize ang isang cost function. Sa modelong ito, ginagamit ng SciPy ang output ng cost function para kalkulahin ang susunod nitong input.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"two-vqe\"></span>\n"
msgstr "<span id=\"two-vqe\"></span>\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Run two VQE algorithms in a session by using threading {#run-two-vqe-algorithms-in-a-session-by-using-threading}"
msgstr "Magpatakbo ng dalawang VQE algorithm sa isang session gamit ang threading {#run-two-vqe-algorithms-in-a-session-by-using-threading}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "You can get more out of a session by running multiple workloads simultaneously. The following example shows how you can run two VQE algorithms, each using a different classical optimizer, simultaneously inside a single session. Job tags are also used to differentiate jobs from each workload.\n"
msgstr "Maaari kang makakuha ng mas marami mula sa isang session sa pamamagitan ng pagpapatakbo ng maraming workload nang sabay-sabay. Ipinapakita ng sumusunod na halimbawa kung paano mo maaaring patakbuhin ang dalawang VQE algorithm, na ang bawat isa ay gumagamit ng ibang klasikal na optimizer, nang sabay-sabay sa loob ng iisang session. Ginagamit din ang mga job tag para matukoy kung aling job ang galing sa bawat workload.\n"

